 10. **DrawComplete & Clip Exclusion** — Raises `DrawComplete`. For opaque views, the entire frame is excluded from the clip. For transparent views, only the actually-drawn cells are excluded. This ensures later-drawn (lower-Z) views don't overwrite this view's content.
 
+### SubView-Only Draws
+
+If a view's own <xref:Terminal.Gui.ViewBase.View.NeedsDraw> is `false` and it is entered only because `SubViewNeedsDraw` is set, the view does **not** redraw itself: steps 1, 3, 5, 6, and 7 are skipped, and only the SubViews that need drawing are drawn (step 4). The view's previously drawn adornments, viewport, text, and content remain in the driver's contents. Overlapped SubViews with `SuperViewRendersLineCanvas = true` that did not redraw contribute the cell map from their last full draw, so LineCanvas compositing (step 8) is unchanged. Clip exclusion (step 10) still happens for every view.
+
+The view falls back to a full draw when a SubView of one of its adornments needs drawing, or when a tiled (non-overlapped) SubView with `SuperViewRendersLineCanvas = true` needs drawing (its lines must auto-join with the view's own lines).
